# This directory is //go:embed'd by server.go, but its contents are
# generated by `npm run build` in the repository root's ui/ (see its
# vite.config.js outDir) -- not checked in, so a stale build can never
# ship instead of a real one. .gitkeep keeps the directory itself
# present on a fresh checkout, since go:embed fails to compile if it's
# missing outright.
#
# That alone isn't enough, though: go:embed's default directory pattern
# also excludes dotfiles, so a fresh checkout -- which has only .gitkeep
# and .gitignore here -- embeds zero files and `go build` fails outright,
# not just at run time. placeholder.html is tracked for exactly that
# case: a non-dotfile so the embed pattern has something to match. It
# can never ship in place of a real build because server.go serves this
# directory with http.FileServerFS: once `npm run build` has written an
# index.html, "/" resolves to that, and this file is reachable only at
# its own path.
#
# `make frontend` (the prerequisite for `make build`/`test`/`vet`, and
# for the container build) clears this directory before running `npm run
# build`, but exempts this file along with the two dotfiles. It used to
# delete it, which mattered because this is the only *tracked* file among
# the three: removing it left the checkout permanently dirty, and
# ../../../scripts/setup.sh's sync_repo refuses to update a dirty
# checkout rather than clobber what might be an operator's edit -- so on
# a host that builds in place from a git clone, the first successful
# build broke every deploy after it.
*
!.gitignore
!.gitkeep
!placeholder.html
